{"name":"Alto","hex":"#cdc6c5","fetched":"2026-10-21","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Alto","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A census-designated place in Marin County, California, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Alto"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alto","blocks":[{"text":"The musical term alto, meaning \"high\" in Italian, historically refers to the contrapuntal part higher than the tenor and its associated vocal range. In four-part voice leading alto is the second-highest part, sung in choruses by either low women's or high men's voices. In vocal classification these are usually called mezzo-soprano, contralto and male alto or countertenor."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alto","wikidata":"Q6983813"},{"title":"Alto (high-speed rail)","blocks":[{"text":"Alto is a planned high-speed rail line in Canada, intended to connect major cities including Toronto, Ottawa, Montreal, and Quebec City. The planning and development of the line is being overseen by a federal Crown corporation operating under the same name which is a wholly owned subsidiary of Via Rail Canada Inc."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alto_(high-speed_rail)","wikidata":"Q115716080"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.60875},{"title":"Palo Alto Baylands January 2013 004 edit","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Palo_Alto_Baylands_January_2013_004_edit.jpg/500px-Palo_Alto_Baylands_January_2013_004_edit.jpg","ratio":2,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palo_Alto_Baylands_January_2013_004_edit.jpg","share":0.464375},{"title":"Palo Alto 1945","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Palo_Alto_1945.jp